      {
        "id": 21355,
        "name": "evandan457",
        "username": "evandan457",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/e/5e9695/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2011-09-23T14:34:39.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"&quot;&quot;Veet&quot;&quot;\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n \"\"Veet\"\":</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>I can’t help but notice that in Visionary’s back story here on the site it mentions and evil copy of Visionary existing somewhere within her mind.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I’m pretty sure it’s safe to assume that her evil copy is definitely going to come back, and I’m guessing that thing on Visionary’s flip side is that evil copy. Whether it will be her nemesis or not, I don’t know.</p>\n<p>And since everyone seems to look at the cards to look for the heroes’ possible nemeses, I took a look at Bunker’s deck and came up with two ideas. First, on his “Flak Cannon” card, there seems to be what I can only describe as a dark-skinned giant wearing a cowcatcher on his head. He seems like a good match against Bunker, considering he’s taking a flak cannon to the shoulder pretty well. Or, also in Bunker’s deck is the “Decommissioned Hardware” card. it shows three of the old Bunker suits, and so maybe some military-related villain might steal those and use one of them (or all of them – squad of Bunker-suited minions led by evil general?).</p>\n<p>Haka’s nemesis had better be the Hippoman from Haka’s “Savage Mana”. WE WANT HIPPOMAN.</p>\n<p>I know someone already said this, but to say it again: Ra’s nemesis, beyond any doubt in my mind, will be the Anubis on Ra’s “Scorched Earth” card. If that’s not Ra’s nemesis, I will be genuinely shocked.</p>",
